#N canvas 20 20 1700 1500 12;
#X text 20 20 e_verb -- the drums' one reverb \, in c_kit: each track's send \, and its size \, damping and type \, the kit's (Brendan \, 2026-11-05). Three engines \, each behind the same controls: plate \, gigaverb and freeverb \, each in its own switch~ \, so only the chosen one runs. mono. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 150 creation arg: c_kit's \$0 \, for the throws. In: the tracks' sends \, thrown to \$1-verb by every c_voice and e_delay. inlet: send <pad> <0-100> \, every track's send \, size <0-100> \, damping <0-100> and type <0-2> \, 0 plate \, 1 gigaverb \, 2 freeverb \, from c_steps through c_kit. Out: the reverb alone \, wet \, thrown to c_kit's \$1-out by the engines., f 70;
#X obj 1000 300 inlet;
#X obj 1000 340 route send size damping type;
#X obj 20 700 e_plate \$1 \$0;
#X obj 320 700 e_gigaverb \$1 \$0;
#X obj 620 700 e_freeverb \$1 \$0;
#X obj 1000 420 array define \$0-sends 16;
#X obj 1000 460 unpack f f;
#X obj 1150 540 f;
#X obj 1000 500 - 1;
#X obj 1000 540 t b b f;
#X obj 1150 580 tabwrite \$0-sends;
#X obj 1000 620 array sum \$0-sends;
#X obj 1000 660 > 0;
#X obj 1300 420 clip 0 2;
#X obj 1300 460 t b f;
#X obj 1000 740 expr \$f1 * (\$f2 == 0)\; \$f1 * (\$f2 == 1)\; \$f1 * (\$f2 == 2);
#X msg 1000 780 want \$1;
#X msg 1160 780 want \$1;
#X msg 1320 780 want \$1;
#X msg 1000 860 size \$1;
#X obj 1000 900 t a a a;
#X msg 1200 860 damping \$1;
#X obj 1200 900 t a a a;
#X obj 1000 1000 array define \$0-on 3;
#X obj 1000 1080 unpack f f;
#X msg 20 760 0 \$1;
#X msg 320 760 1 \$1;
#X msg 620 760 2 \$1;
#X obj 1150 1160 f;
#X obj 1000 1120 t b b f;
#X obj 1150 1200 tabwrite \$0-on;
#X obj 1000 1240 array sum \$0-on;
#X obj 1000 1280 > 0;
#X obj 1000 1320 change;
#X obj 1000 1360 switch~;
#X obj 20 300 catch~ \$1-verb;
#X obj 20 340 s~ \$0-in;
#X text 20 860 Each engine takes the sends from \$0-in \, at its own gain while it is wanted \, and throws the reverb to c_kit's \$1-out. An engine is wanted while it is the type and any send is above 0: so a change of type stops the old one taking input \, and it rings out \, then switches off \; the two run together only for that tail. Their gains match their levels: a send is as loud in each., f 60;
#X text 20 1060 switch~: on while any engine is \, each turning its own on while it is wanted and off once its tail has been below -80 dBFS for 300 ms (e_tail). So with every send at 0 and every tail died \, nothing of the reverb runs. A switch~ starts off. While it is off every throw to it is zeros \, every send being 0 \, so the catch~ never fills up., f 60;
#X text 1300 1000 size \, damping and type each start at their starting points in the engines' boxes \, 50 \, 50 and plate \, and are not set at load: c_steps tells c_kit every effect's value at load (ref/module/sequencer.md)., f 40;
